WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.340
We're back ladies and gentlemen with episode 2 of the supremely mind-bending "Maniac",

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.980
so take your pills and settle in because it's gonna get weird.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.060
Well episode 1 focused on Owen,

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.220
episode 2 focuses on Annie.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.820
Here in her apartment, we're struck with a vast contrast

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.200
from the structured businesslike world of Owen Milgram,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.920
clutter adorns the room and highlighted is a book of modern art,

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.828
not surprising considering a 2013 study from the University of Minnesota concluded that

00:00:27.828 --> 00:00:31.240
those that keep cluttered houses are often more creative.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.720
Annie pulls out a pill bottle and has a few harsh words with the last remaining tablet,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.080
shaped like an "A" before crushing it and snorting the residue like cocaine.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.952
What follows is a seemingly euphoric experience,

00:00:42.952 --> 00:00:46.900
seen in fast motion as a roommates blur about their day around her.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.789
You'll notice here more rainbow imagery harkening back to Neberdine.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.919
Annie awakens from her high with a tear rolling down her face as Flash Gordon plays on the TV.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:02.540
She pulls out a cigar box where we see her copy of Don Quixote that she pulled from the trash in episode 1,

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:06.380
inferring the events here take place after the opening of that episode.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.780
We get a view of scars on Annie's back,

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.298
a reference to the events at the end of this episode,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.620
as she pulls out a picture who will later learn is her sister Ellie,

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.420
before getting to work on a lost dog poster.

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:22.200
She glares once more at the pill bottle and we get a few more clues as to where it came from.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.740
More Japanese lettering and the words saying

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.951
"trial ULP phase 3"

00:01:26.951 --> 00:01:31.040
confirming its connection to NBP and Owen's ULP screening.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.629
There's also the letter "A", like the pill,

00:01:33.629 --> 00:01:35.240
and "this is a test".

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:39.480
Outside, Annie puts up the lost dog posters and we get a look at her creation.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.900
Might be a little too late looking for a dog lost seven years ago, but take note of the woman in the picture.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.840
It's her sister, not her.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.979
At a noodle shop, Annie takes in a few ads from "Ad Buddy".

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:55.160
I'm guessing this is how Annie paid for her meal, as well later learn she's having trouble paying the rent.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.300
When buddy here mentions the limitless options they can offer,

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.080
Annie expresses a desire to reach Salt Lake City to see her sister,

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.420
and wonders if "Ad Buddy" could pay the way,

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.080
buddy says it should only take a few thousand ads.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:07.760
Hikes!

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.840
Back home, Annie packs a bag and picks up Don Quixote,

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.920
claiming she's "healthy Annie" now,

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.040
no more pills.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.600
It's no coincidence that Don Quixote is referenced so much,

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.500
the stories of a noble who loses his sanity reading too many chivalrous romances,

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.640
and takes on a quest to revive chivalry.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:30.840
Don Quixote does not see the world as it really is and prefers to imagine he is living out a knightly story.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.140
Sound like anyone we know?

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.128
However, Annie's quest to reach Salt Lake City is thwarted due to lack of funds,

00:02:36.128 --> 00:02:38.260
and she pays a visit to her dad Hank,

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.040
a cross between Hal from 2001 a Space Odyssey

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.540
and a vampire coffin.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:48.360
Hank has hidden away from the world in an "a-void", seemingly as a way of avoiding his problems,

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.280
mainly the sorrow he feels from Annie's mother's passing.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.840
I'm also getting big Back to the Future vibes from these numbers, yet another homage to the 80s.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.340
Annie hits up dad's safe for some bus money and we see a gun.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.660
Could this be the same gun she makes reference to in episode 1?

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.220
She becomes a visibly upset,

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.600
which is no surprise considering her dad has locked himself away.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:13.120
But this doesn't seem to stop her from taking a lot more than a few bucks for the bus.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.720
With cash in hand, she grabs her bag and heads out.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.760
Notice the same style painting here in her apartment, as in her dad's place.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.691
Before entering the terminal, we get a glimpse

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.600
at the Soldiers and Sailors Arch at Grand Army Plaza in Brooklyn,

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.460
that has been covered in neon lights.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.037
Inside the bus terminal, Annie purchases a ticket to Salt Lake City,

00:03:31.037 --> 00:03:33.680
but hallucinates while looking at the rolling bus numbers,

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.060
the entire board forms the letter "A".

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.680
While Owens issues stem from his schizophrenia,

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.040
Annie seems to be an addiction to this mysterious "A" drug.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.500
The drug has won this day, and she needs more.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.070
At Washington Square Park, Annie meets up with her supplier, Calvin.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:53.340
He's playing a classic game of New York chess with a purple robotic gambling koala.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.820
Turns out "pill-A" isn't something you can just order whenever you want.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.920
Calvin snatched it from his dad who works for NBP,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.353
and can't get her anymore.

00:04:01.353 --> 00:04:06.580
Annie pleads for a lead, but he tells her NBP has gotten way more secretive since the suicides,

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.689
but after Annie drop some bus money

00:04:08.689 --> 00:04:12.740
he gives the name of Neberdine's intake director, Patricia Lugo.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.020
Annie visits "dox stop",

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.580
an establishment which helps find dirt on others

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.360
by gaining access to people's personal information.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:23.580
It's essentially the opposite of the identity stolen ad from episode 1,

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.940
and wouldn't you love the irony of the same ad off to the side here.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.900
Inside, Annie drops more of her dad's cash to blackmail Patricia Lugo,

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.820
looks like they don't take "Ad Buddy" in exchange for doxing.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.620
Apparently Patricia has a disorderly arrest on her record,

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.120
was a gambler, and lost custody of her daughter,

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.340
then had it all scrubbed,

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.620
so she could get her job at Neberdine.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.740
For a fee, Mr. Dox says he'll even threaten to kidnap a kid,

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.640
"that shit always works".

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.700
Instead, he finds she's a user of something called "Friend Proxy",

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.160
for pretend friends,

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.920
a service not unlike "Daddy's Home" where someone fills in as your friend.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:59.100
It's clear this world is really painted as one of loneliness,

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.100
people lacking connection.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.640
Annie Intercepts Patricia at a Botanical Garden,

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.020
notice all the bonsai trees which make a number of appearances at the NBP labs.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.732
She pretends to be her proxy friend, Juanita,

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.420
and noticed the friend proxy pin she wears,

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.480
just like the man from episode 1.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.002
But after a slip-up in her story

00:05:17.002 --> 00:05:19.460
and a glance over at two young girls in the garden,

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.980
perhaps reminding Annie of herself and her sister,

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.420
she gives up the goat and retreats.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:28.650
If you recall, this young girl here is Owen's niece that we saw at episode 1.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.900
"How did you know?"

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.480
But rather than counting herself lucky and leaving,

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.940
Patricia follows Annie, maybe that's how desperate for a human connection she is.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.960
Annie explains the reasons she blackmailed Patricia is to get into the Neberdine trials

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.840
because she needs more of those pills,

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.580
the only thing that makes her feel better about her relationship with her sister.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.000
She describes a cold rock that has been left in her stomach

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.200
by an argument they have five years ago.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.620
Patricia tells her she could reach out to her sister,

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.620
but Annie says "I can't."

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:02.680
The story works and Annie gets to take the defence mechanism tests that Owen did in episode 1.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.780
Here, she gives answers she thinks the screener wants to hear

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.620
such as super-happy and togetherness.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:14.460
Perhaps the only response close to a real one is her reaction of sisters making faces at each other.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.880
The screener then does the final stare down,

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.580
but Annie just holds, her vitals rising before getting the red light,

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.420
guess her defence mechanisms weren't fungible.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:28.100
A pissed-off Annie decides to take Mr. Dox's original advice and blackmail Patricia,

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.460
saying if she doesn't get into her study, she'll never see her daughter again.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.445
Guess he was right,

00:06:32.445 --> 00:06:33.860
"that shit always works".

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:38.820
Now the story starts to connect from episode 1 as we cut to Owens staring Annie down.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:45.360
He heads in for his ULP test while Patricia upgrades another tester to a much much safer trial,

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.360
and hands Annie her golden ticket.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.133
We arrive back in the pot room

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:53.320
and are treated to an introduction video in our first look at Dr. Mantleray,

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:57.760
played here by Justin Theroux who does a fantastic job of bad-acting.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:01.760
His last name you might remember from the ad Annie passes in episode 1.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.920
Could Greta Mantelray be his mother?

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.260
I gotta say this was one of my favorite parts of the whole episode,

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.560
the 80s VHS style effects,

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.420
the specific cuts made in the video.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.060
"No one sees inside your head"

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:14.780
says Dr. Morimoto assuredly,

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.040
than six seconds later

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.360
"but us."

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.200
The videos purpose is to explain how the test works,

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.740
and it's simple,

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:23.820
three pills taken in three steps

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:29.900
analyzed by the most sophisticated mega computer ever developed, the G.R.T.A.,

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.800
eerily similar to Greta.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.152
After ingesting the pills,

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:35.960
the machines cutting-edge artificial intelligence will

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.060
identify,

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:37.680
map, and

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.080
confront the learned programming of your brain.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.400
Simple right?

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:45.980
Pill-A, Annie's pill is called "Agonia", which in Greek translates to

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:50.000
"of severe mental struggles and emotions, agony, anguish".

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:55.560
This pill pulls at your core traumas and worst memories of your life and maps them for pill B and C.

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:58.520
"But don't worry, it's safe."

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:03.640
Pill-B, "Behavioral", identifies your minds defence mechanisms and blind spots.

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:04.779
"Your blind spots!"

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:07.820
Pill-C, "Confricia", "Confrontation",

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:12.840
the end of the rainbow, likely why we've seen so many rainbows referenced throughout the show.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.860
Once pill A and B have worked,

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.980
G.R.T.A. will remap your brain and voila, you're cured! Simple, right?

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.640
Dr. Morimoto asks if anyone has questions,

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.367
and then ignores the ones who do

00:08:23.367 --> 00:08:27.360
and lets the evens know they're going to get a delicious pre-weighed meal,

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.600
while the odds hit the microwave chairs.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:33.700
As Annie lines up for the tests, we get a look into Dr. Fujita's control room.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.721
Notice some of the shoulders of the workers who have yellow stripes

00:08:36.721 --> 00:08:39.460
and the one man on the right who has blue or indigo

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:44.520
suggesting the rainbow colors of MBP separate into different departments of the company.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:48.720
In the lineup, Owen tells Annie everyone thought he was crazy, but they were wrong.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.780
Annie replies, they'll talk about this later.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:54.100
She's going along with him as to not attract attention.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:58.020
In the supercomputer room, we find. Dr. Morimoto reading a poem to G.R.T.A.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:02.820
It's William Blake's the angel poem, suggesting that she is seen as a guardian angel.

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:07.800
It seems like G.R.T.A. is more complex than a regular computer and enjoys this poetry,

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.240
almost as if she has emotions.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.780
Later, Dr. Fujita implies G.R.T.A.'s safety-net is connected to how much she liked the poem.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:19.580
The odds get placed in their chairs and are donned with x-ray vests, straight out of your dentist's office.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.580
Dr. Fujita addresses her crew and explains

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.120
the test subject's data over the next three days is vital to their success

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.180
and that the subjects lives are in their hands,

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.260
no more mistakes.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:32.980
"Don't worry, it's safe."

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.960
Finally, Annie gets her pill and the Machine fires up.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:39.400
Electrical wires get sent from the chairs to the computer.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:42.660
Wires depicting the connection from each participant can be seen,

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.040
with 1 being Owen, and 9 being Annie.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.660
Dr. Fujita instructs the crew to be gentle, and that hard-entry is their enemy.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.800
In Annie's mind, we see a Dutch windmill.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.112
"Windmill" being the title of this episode and a sign saying

00:09:55.112 --> 00:09:57.320
"leave to the nightingale her shady woods"

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:01.520
this is a reference to William Wordsworth's poem called "To a Skylark".

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:06.000
The poem itself about a skylark's connection to its roots, while also flying high.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.260
But of interest is the line "leave to the nightingale her shady wood",

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.680
the nightingale is a songbird that, unlike the skylark, keeps to the woods.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.680
Is Annie our nightingale and her sister the skylark?

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.569
In this memory, Annie pumped some gas

00:10:19.569 --> 00:10:23.180
and sports a new short hairdo as her sister Ellie comes from inside.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.220
We can assume this memory is at least five years or older,

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:31.620
as we know from the earlier conversation with Patricia that this is how long it's been since the two last spoke.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:34.800
And considering this is a pill-A memory, aka Agonia,

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:38.560
it's also likely the origin of Annie and her sisters falling out.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.100
Cute sister hijinks ensue.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:45.060
That night in a motel room, the two gloss over their tumultuous relationship with their mother

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.680
and escaped into fantasy.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:52.580
Ellie explains her moved to Salt Lake City is because of her fiancé and opens up about her fears of stability.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:56.000
She's afraid she'll screw it up and this screw up her future kids,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.860
just like what happened to the sisters.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:00.840
But in this fantasy Ellie explains she doesn't screw up,

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.480
she has her happy ending.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:05.571
Rather than act supportive, Annie pushes back and they argue.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.900
Ellie brings up the fact that Annie can't take care of anything,

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.800
which Annie assumes is a reference to Ellie's dog,

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.320
inferring that she lost him.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.100
They sling more insults, calling each other "mom",

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:19.740
and Annie gets mean by stating how happy she is that Ellie is moving far away.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.301
The next morning, Annie begins a careful attempt to reconcile

00:11:23.301 --> 00:11:25.940
and decides to take a serious picture with her sister.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:28.660
Ellie holds the wheel as Annie goes to take a selfie,

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.600
but eventually, Annie makes another joke of it.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:36.200
As the to grapple over the camera a truck comes barreling down the wrong side of the road,

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.880
and plows into them, sending Annie and Ellie over the side of the road.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:44.160
Annie is flung from her car and lives while her sister is left to die in the wreckage below.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:47.920
Thus why Annie explained she can't reconcile to Lugo.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:48.900
Here amongst the blood,

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:52.078
you can also see the fresh scar wounds on Annie's back

00:11:52.078 --> 00:11:55.160
the same place her scars were seen at the beginning of the episode.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.170
Back in the test room,

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:58.870
we see a crying Annie similar to what happened on her couch

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.680
the last time she took the pill.

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:02.500
Pill-A has located her trauma,

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.060
but what kind of effect has the pill had on Owen's brain?

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:08.220
And what will pills B and C have for them down the line?

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:09.399
Thanks again for watching.

00:12:09.399 --> 00:12:12.300
If you liked this series, please make sure to like and share it.

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:16.900
There's a whole lot more to unpack in the upcoming episodes. So I hope you'll join me...

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.440
until next time.

